# Production deploy verification — batches 1-9 merged to main — 2026-10-25

Scope: branch opencode/batch9 (28 commits, faeb006..cdc8eab) fast-forward merged
into main and pushed. Both platforms already served the new code at first probe
(Vercel/Railway had evidently been tracking opencode/batch9 from the earlier
same-day push of cdc8eab); the main push makes the production branch canonical.

## Migration state (prerequisite check)

Raw output of `npx prisma migrate deploy` against production over the
transaction pooler (port 6543, pgbouncer=true, connection_limit=1; the session
pooler on 5432 was persistently EMAXCONNSESSION-exhausted by the live backend's
pool — retried 5x over ~2 min before switching, see "Known environment gotchas"):

    Datasource "db": PostgreSQL database "postgres", schema "public" at "aws-0-eu-west-1.pooler.supabase.com:6543"
    35 migrations found in prisma/migrations
    No pending migrations to apply.

=> Production schema already current, including 20261024000000_add_submitted_at
   and all ten earlier batch migrations. No Railway stop was needed.

## Backend probes (https://hamame-platform-production.up.railway.app/api)

Unauthenticated discriminators (new route => standard 401 shape, old backend
=> 404 NOT_FOUND). Raw bodies:

    GET  /plans                  -> 200  {"plans":[{"id":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000100","name":"free",...
    GET  /authoring/me/drafts    -> 401  {"error":{"code":"UNAUTHENTICATED","message":"A Bearer token is required for this endpoint."}}
    GET  /points/balance         -> 401  {"error":{"code":"UNAUTHENTICATED","message":"A Bearer token is required for this endpoint."}}
    GET  /groups                 -> 401  {"error":{"code":"UNAUTHENTICATED","message":"A Bearer token is required for this endpoint."}}
    GET  /dms                    -> 401  {"error":{"code":"UNAUTHENTICATED","message":"A Bearer token is required for this endpoint."}}
    GET  /progress/readiness     -> 401  {"error":{"code":"UNAUTHENTICATED","message":"A Bearer token is required for this endpoint."}}
    POST /ai/explain-answer      -> 401  {"error":{"code":"UNAUTHENTICATED","message":"A Bearer token is required for this endpoint."}}

Path corrections during probing (my initial guesses were wrong, not gaps):
- DMs mount at /api/dms (src/routes/index.ts:96), not /api/messages.
- Readiness is /api/progress/readiness (progress.routes.ts:291), not /api/readiness.

## Frontend probes (https://hamame-platform-wcpk.vercel.app)

    GET / -> 200
    GET /ai-chat -> 200        GET /points -> 200
    GET /groups -> 200         GET /messages -> 200
    GET /internships -> 200    GET /associations -> 200
    GET /authoring -> 200

All new client pages from the batch range serve the app shell (200), where the
pre-batch deployment would 404 (e.g. /ai-chat, /points, /groups did not exist).

## What is NOT verified live (honest limits)

- Any authenticated flow (passwords rotated 2026-09-12, not in repo). Owner
  click-through needed for: practice-player AI explain panel, study chat,
  review-queue submittedAt sort (reviewer login), readiness
  recommendedNextSession rendering, authoring drafts list.
- GEMINI_API_KEY is NOT set on Railway (deliberate warn-only policy). Until the
  owner adds it, AI features degrade gracefully instead of calling the model.
  Local pre-deploy equivalents were verified: verify:explain 16/16 (offline
  mode), verify:credits 13/13, plus the browser e2e under next start
  (docs/verification/2026-10-24-explain-panel-e2e.log).

## Remaining owner action

Add GEMINI_API_KEY in the Railway service Variables (triggers a redeploy).
